Vault CLI – Simple Secure Password Manager
Vault CLI is a lightweight, terminal-based password manager written in Go. It securely stores your passwords in an encrypted file using a 32-byte encryption key. All data is stored locally and never leaves your machine.

Features
AES-256 encryption for all stored data

Add, retrieve, delete, and list password entries from the command line

Generate strong random passwords

No cloud dependency – your secrets, your control

Getting Started
1. Clone the Repository
    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/vault-cli.git

2. Generate a Secure 32-Byte Key
    Before using Vault CLI, you must generate a secure 32-byte key.
    Run the following Python script:
    import secrets
    import string
    alphabet = string.ascii_letters + string.digits
    key = ''.join(secrets.choice(alphabet) for _ in range(32))
    print(key)
    Copy the printed key and save it in a secure place.
    You will need this key to access your vault.

3. Set the VAULT_KEY Environment Variable
    export VAULT_KEY= key
    Replace with the key you generated in the previous step.

4. Build and Run
    make build 
    make install // Please edit the MAKEFILE to add your PATH.
